	)
	(text "PG_HVAUX is driven actively high by AUX-HV when good (interfaces.AUX): 100k pull-down\nhere, so a dead or unplugged AUX-HV reads not-good. 10k + BAT54S clamp toward CTRL."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 255.05 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7e3d1fa5-1271-5978-9f58-92343d5e44a4")
	)
	(text "LM74800 + 2 x CSD18532Q5B back-to-back (common drain): ideal diode (DGATE) + load disconnect (HGATE).\nConnects only when NO cabinet feed is healthy (priority detector holds EN/UVLO in shutdown): cabinet healthy\nabove 20.85-21.41 V rising, lost below 20.37-21.20 V falling (any in-window cabinet wins, INT-10). AUX UVLO\n20.09-21.49 V rising / 18.34-19.66 V falling; AUX OV 23.97-25.57 V, re-arm below 21.88-23.39 V: a failed AUX-HV\n(23.8-28.5 V) is cut off before the 26.13 V bus cut-off and stays off (INT-08). AUX-HV overshoot must stay\n< 23.97 V. While AUX_EN is up, sheet 08 forces fans, +24V_GD and 24V_DO off, latched (D-022, <= 30 W).\nHGATE ramp (LM7480-Q1 fig 9-3): R1 1k + CdVdT 2.2u 100 V X7R; a disabled HGATE sits at OUT, so CdVdT tracks the\nbus. Black start: 0.016-0.063 V/ms, one ramp in 0.39-1.53 s, AUX-HV <= 38.0 W (limit 39.8 W), > 34 W for <= 60\nms (timer >= 88 ms). Cabinet -> AUX: inhibit <= 0.17 ms, HGATE on <= 1.08 ms, FET conducts <= 5.98 ms after\nthe detector releases; bus >= 16.32 V > logic UVLO 15.48 V (+24V eFuse) at 27.8 W. AUX -> cabinet: AUX off\n~35 us, bus falls to the cabinet - no gap; +24V_GD / 24V_DO stay off until FLT_CLR."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 200.01 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "848e662a-675d-53f4-9764-2384e99095fe")
	)
